# Consumerism

Consumerism as a historical and cultural force that has shaped modern society and business practices.

## Historical Development
The book traces the historical development of consumerism and how it has shaped modern society, setting the context for understanding current societal and economic dynamics. Consumerism reflects the human psychology behind capitalism—our inherent desire to succeed drives businesses but also creates potential pitfalls when unchecked by ethical considerations.

## Effects
- Shaping of modern society and business priorities
- Driving innovation but also leading to unsustainable practices
- Deepening social divides through unequal access to consumption
- Environmental degradation from relentless profit pursuit

## Connection to Galloway's Work
Relates to [[the-four]] on how consumer platforms dominate markets and [[scott-galloway]]'s broader analysis of business strategy.

